 say for example  monday from  time a to time b there's a block of time  where i have 30 minute meetings back to  back to back to back with every single  person on my team  and what i'm doing is i'm basically  level setting for the week here's what  we did last week here's what our  challenges are here's what's going well  and here's what we're going to do for  this week  and we should go through that in that  block of time that compartment of time  i then have content days for example so  on wednesday and thursday afternoons  from about one o'clock to five o'clock i  sit down and all i do is i focus on  output of content usually for the  podcast and so when i do that i'm  compartmentalizing it i know going into  wednesday and thursday afternoons  that's all i'm focused on and so by  compartmentalizing your time you can  become hyper efficient  but you also can plan out exactly when  you're gonna get everything done  and so when you start to think about how  much time we actually have  what you find is one people are super  inefficient but also two  people don't have a plan and therefore  don't get done what they need to  because they simply weren't prepared but  i'm a huge believer that if you plan  correctly you'll end up actually  accomplishing what you want and that's  the  strategy that i use and it's worked out  so far so i just kind of keep doubling  and tripling down on it and improving  that process but that's basically it  just compartmentalize your time and then  stick to a disciplined schedule  what's up guys bang bang i hope you're  enjoying this conversation but before we  go any further i want to quickly tell  you about today's sponsor  blockfy blockfi has got four different  financial products for crypto investors  you can deposit crypto and earn up to  eight point six percent apy  in an interest bearing account you can  deposit crypto and take out a us dollar  loan against your crypto collateral  you can use their cryptocurrency  exchange and have n