st use of my  time and so you just have to get  very very comfortable with the idea that  you may be disappointing people or you  may be offending people even though you  don't mean to  it's just simply at some point there's a  trade-off between accomplishing what you  want versus always serving everybody  else  and you just got to find that balance  wherever you're comfortable um  crypto chris wants to know when will you  run for office  short answer never uh that sounds  horrendous  uh i really really like my life i'm  gonna keep my life the way that it is  uh the idea of being a politician is  uh frankly like nauseating to me uh one  of the things that i always uh kind of  go back to is this framework of  in the country today are you more likely  to have an impact  as a private citizen in either business  or investing  or as a politician my guess actually is  that you  can have more impact as a business  person or as an investor  than you can as a politician in the  current environment and so just from a  pure impact standpoint  uh being in the private market is going  to be much much more advantageous for  creating change or  or kind of making any sort of progress  than actually sitting inside of a  bureaucratic institution  and maybe that changes over time but  even if it did change i still  really am a big believer of uh kind of  that public spotlight and scrutiny and  the mudslinging that happens in politics  which is very antithetical to the way  that i want to live my life  uh and the way that i kind of think  about engaging with those around me in  terms of creating progress or any sort  of innovation and so  the private market is something that i'm  really interested in uh and it's kind of  where i'll stay forever  i really don't see that being an  attractive path of going in  and wearing a suit in time being a  politician speak for yourself i would  make a wonderful first lady  um rand milstein asks  when a bitcoin movie is gonna be made  who will play  